ness in the chaos Trejo  hit a prison official in the head with a  rock a crime that got him tossed into  solitary confinement  Trejo spent over three months in  solitary acting out movies like The  Wizard of Oz and the Hunchback of Notre  Dom to keep saying realizing he needed  to get his life straightened out he  started to pray saying God if you're  there everything will be alright if  you're not I'm screwed  miraculously the charges against him  were dropped and he slowly but surely  began to rehabilitate himself Trejo also  turned his life around by Knuckle endow  ninh getting sober  he started using marijuana at age eight  and shooting heroin at age twelve and he  also consumed a whole lot of alcohol in  his early days determined to set things  right  he joined Alcoholics Anonymous and  Narcotics Anonymous and today he has  been sober for nearly 50 years and after  he was released from prison he decided  to lend a hand to his fellow man working  as a drug counselor for 15 years today  he is still counseling people in  speaking to at-risk youth  Trejo kept himself pretty busy after  leaving prison in 1969 working as both a  drug counselor and a court liaison but  he was forced to do all sorts of things  to pay the bills  he tried becoming a boxer but when his  license was denied he picked up some  pocket change by throwing down in  smokers aka unsanctioned matches he also  earned a living by working at a wrecking  yard before teaming up with a friend to  start his very own enterprise the two  opened a gardening business but while  they had plenty of get-up-and-go they  didn't have all the necessary equipment  they didn't even have a lawn mower  however trios tough times were soon all  about to change  in 1985 Trejo was working as a drug  counselor when he got a call from a  client who desperately needed help this  guy was working on the set of runaway  train a prison thriller starring Jon  Voight and Eric Roberts and he was  struggling with an urge to use cocaine  Trejo showed up on the set to give the  guys some assistance but it wasn't long  before someone approached Trejo and  asked if he'd like to be an extra in the  movie he took the job but as he was  changing into his outfit screenwriter  Eddie bunker spotted his chest tattoo  bunker had also served time and when he  saw the cowgirl ink  he remembered Trey hos boxing behind  bars it was an amazing coincidence  especially since the filmmakers were  looking for someone to teach Eric  Roberts how to fight I know what's at  bay and he said 320 a day  Trejo gave the actor a few pointers  which so impressed the director that he  offered Trejo a much bigger parts as the  guy who squares off against Roberts on  screen and then I remember he kissed me  give me a kiss on this cheek and in case  Andrei Konchalovsky a Russian man I  remember telling air-air Eddie  bonkers Eddie look I'm gonna do this  training for 320 but if I'm gonna be  kissing his old man  Oh more money it was tray hose first  roll the one that kick-started his  entire acting career and it was all  thanks to that Wilde tattoo ever since  runaway train Trejo has been keeping  himself pretty busy visit his IMDB page  and you'll find he's got over 300  credits in his filmography during his  30-plus years of acting he's starred  alongside some of the biggest action  stars in the business like Charles  Bronson Steven Seagal and Chuck Norris  Trejo has also appeared in some of the  biggest thrillers of all time  he played Johnny 23 in Conair a movie he  once described as the biggest case of  testosterone I've ever been in he also  showed up in the Michael Mann classic  heat as the appropriately named Trejo a  member of Robert De Niro's criminal crew  other notable credits include xxx six  days seven nights anaconda and The  Devil's Rejects plus if you've ever  turned on a TV you've no doubt seen  Trejo and shows like the x-files  Baywatch Sons of Anarchy Breaking Bad  and even the soap opera The Young and  the Restless in addition to action  flicks he's also done kid movies like  Muppets Most Wanted and comedies like  anchorman and you're gonna have to learn  how to deal with it right  are you saying something look I don't  speak Spanish cinema is full of  fantastic actor director collaborations  and Danny Trejo and Robert Rodriguez  deserve to be considered among the most  legendary pairs the two first met while  working on desperado where Rodriguez was  struck by Trey hos natural magnetism  strangely enough while working on the  film they discovered that they are  actually second cousins where do these  crazy ideas come from and after their  first film the two quickly formed a  personal and professional bond that  would lead to nine movies including Spy  Kids and from dusk till dawn but it's  safe to say the two are best known for  working on machete the 2010 exploitation  flick that definitively made Danny Trejo  a household name  rodriguez was inspired to make this nut  so be pitcher from pretty much the first  moment he laid eyes on Trejo he  envisioned his star is the quote Mexican  jean-claude Van Damme or Charles Bronson  and thus he transformed into the  machete-wielding vigilante we now know  and love you could have at least texted  me one chapter don't take once you  become the toughest star in Hollywood  where do you go next if you're Trejo you  go into the restaurant business with the  help of two partners the action star  recently founded his own culinary  Kingdom with locations across Los  Angeles if you're in the mood for  Mexican cuisine you can stop by Trey  hosts tacos if you want coffee and  churros you can drop in to Trey hosts  coffee and donuts and if you fancy a  proper drink with your meal you can  swing by Trey hos cantinas Trey hos  restaurants have vegan vegetarian and  gluten-free options and the actor makes  sure that nothing goes to waste with all  leftovers taken to a homeless shelter  Trey hos food is so good that it was  featured on Anthony Bourdain's show  parts unknown and the late great chef  had nothing but praise for the Mexican  cuisine if you live outside California  you might have to wait a bit before you  can buy yourself a lowrider donuts but  the actor has plans to open locations in  San Antonio Las Vegas and New York  everybody knows that under his  intimidating exterior Danny Trejo is a  big old softy he's a dad a drug  counselor a dude who gives food to the  homeless and naturally he's also a  big-time dog lover  in fact he's such a fan of our  four-legged friends that he's dedicated  countless hours to making the world a  safer place for pets with his ex-wife  Debbie Trejo founded a group called  canine compassion a rescue organization  that emphasizes the importance of  spaying and neutering the actor has  worked with various groups like Best  Friends Animal Society and the  Villalobos rescue center he's spoken  with high school students about proper  pet care and he's appeared in ads for  animal foundations and like any  dedicated dog lover Trejo believes in  adoption as of 2016 he had four cute  canines of his own even though Trejo is  one macho man he has his limits when it  comes to screen action in fact he's very  opinionated when it comes to the topic  of stunt work after Tom Cruise injured  himself filming mission  we'll fall out Trejo told Yahoo movies I  know that all the big stars hate me to  say this but I don't want to risk 80  people's jobs just to say I've got big  huevos on The Tonight Show  according to Trejo it's irresponsible  for a leading man or woman to jeopardize  a film shoot in order to crawl up  buildings or hold on to the side of  planes if the lead gets injured that  might ruin the entire film and then  everybody loses a paycheck Trejo may  seem like a scary guy on the big screen  but in reality he has a heart of gold  knowing full well that he packed some  serious celebrity clouds he does his  best to make a difference wherever he  goes that means working is a drug  intervention counselor fighting for  autism awareness and appearing in PSAs  to promote good manners on the LA metro  and to support male caregivers Trejo is  also incredibly serious about prison  reform going so far as to produce a 2018  documentary called survivors guide to  prison Trejo also appears in the film to  analyze the problems with the US legal  system talk about the abuse that goes on  behind bars and discuss the cases of two  men who were wrongly convicted and  incarcerated as a guy who's been on the  inside he knows a thing or two about how  cruel prison can be and how authority  figures are often indifferent to the  inmate struggling to survive Danny Trejo  is a man who likes to keep busy  and he does a whole lot more than just  appear on the silver screen for example  he's provided voices for multiple video  games  he's also recently promoted the online  shooter guns of boom train has also been  a notable star of music videos he goes  full-on psycho and Slayers pride in  prejudice and throws back some shots and  Enrique Iglesias is loco he gets pushed  around by the Jonas Brothers and burning  up and gives off serious machete vibes  and trains angel and blue jeans  in other words you don't have to look  very far to find Danny Trejo because  he's pretty much everywhere  [Music]
 

